---
import IDELayout from '@layouts/IDELayout.astro';
import FileExplorer from '@components/FileExplorer.astro';
import FileIcon from '@components/FileIcon.astro';
import '@styles/global.css';
---

<IDELayout title="Rafael Carrión - IDE Resume">
  <!-- Sidebar: File Explorer -->
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    <FileExplorer />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Tabs -->
  <Fragment slot="tabs">
    <div class="tab active" data-file="README.md">
      <FileIcon filename="README.md" />
      <span class="truncate">README.md</span>
      <button class="tab-close" aria-label="Close tab">
        <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path d="M18 6L6 18M6 6L18 18"></path>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Editor Content Area -->
  <div class="editor-content-area">
    <!-- README.md Content -->
    <div class="file-content active" data-content="README.md">
      <div class="markdown-preview max-w-4xl">
        <h1>Welcome to racafe.dev</h1>

        <p>
          Hello! I'm <strong>Rafael Carrión</strong>, a Full-Stack Developer based in Barcelona. This portfolio is
          designed to look and feel like <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/">VS Code</a> — because if you're going to
          read about a developer, why not do it in their natural habitat?
        </p>

        <h2>Quick Start</h2>

        <p>Navigate through the <strong>file explorer</strong> on the left to discover different sections:</p>

        <ul>
          <li><code>README.md</code> — You are here</li>
          <li><code>about.md</code> — Learn more about me</li>
          <li><code>experience.json</code> — My professional journey</li>
          <li><code>skills.ts</code> — Technical toolkit</li>
          <li><code>education.yaml</code> — Education & certifications</li>
          <li><code>contact.tsx</code> — Let's connect</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Features</h2>

        <p>This interactive portfolio includes:</p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>File Explorer</strong> — Click files to open them as tabs</li>
          <li><strong>Tab System</strong> — Multiple files open at once, just like a real IDE</li>
          <li><strong>Dark+ Theme</strong> — The classic VS Code look</li>
          <li><strong>Syntax Highlighting</strong> — Code displayed with proper colors</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>About This Project</h2>

        <p>
          Built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> and styled with
          <a href="https://tailwindcss.com/">Tailwind CSS</a>. The design faithfully recreates VS Code's Dark+ theme
          with attention to the small details: the activity bar icons, the file tree animations, and the status bar at
          the bottom.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>"Any sufficiently advanced portfolio is indistinguishable from an actual IDE."</p>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="tip-box">
          <div class="tip-box-title">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
              <path
                d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm1 15h-2v-6h2v6zm0-8h-2V7h2v2z"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            Tip
          </div>
          <div class="tip-box-content">
            Use the file explorer on the left to navigate, or click on any tab to switch between open files.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- about.md Content -->
    <div class="file-content" data-content="about.md">
      <div class="markdown-preview max-w-4xl">
        <h1>About Me</h1>

        <p>
          Hi there! I'm <strong>Rafael Carrión</strong>, a <strong>Full-Stack Developer</strong> based in
          <strong>Barcelona, Spain</strong>. I'm currently working at
          <a href="https://funditec.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Funditec</a>, where I build web
          applications and solve interesting technical challenges every day.
        </p>

        <h2>What I Do</h2>

        <p>
          I specialize in building modern web applications from the ground up. My work spans the entire stack — from
          crafting intuitive user interfaces to designing robust backend systems and everything in between.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React, Vue.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS</li>
          <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Node.js, Python, REST APIs, GraphQL</li>
          <li><strong>Database:</strong> PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis</li>
          <li><strong>DevOps:</strong> Docker, CI/CD, Cloud Services</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>My Approach</h2>

        <p>
          I believe in writing clean, maintainable code that solves real problems. I'm passionate about developer
          experience, performance optimization, and creating software that people actually enjoy using.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>"The best code is no code at all. The second best is code that's easy to understand and change."</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2>Beyond the Code</h2>

        <p>
          When I'm not coding, you'll find me exploring Barcelona's coffee shops, contributing to open-source projects,
          or tinkering with side projects that may or may not see the light of day.
        </p>

        <h2>Let's Connect</h2>

        <p>I'm always open to interesting conversations and new opportunities. Find me on:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/racafe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a> — Check out my open-source
            work
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/rafaelcarrion" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a> — Professional
            network
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://twitter.com/racafe_dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Twitter/X</a> — Occasional
            tech thoughts
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="tip-box">
          <div class="tip-box-title">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
              <path
                d="M20 4H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v12c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h16c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V6c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zm0 4l-8 5-8-5V6l8 5 8-5v2z"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            Get in Touch
          </div>
          <div class="tip-box-content">
            Want to work together or just say hi? Check out <code>contact.tsx</code> in the file explorer for my contact form.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- skills.ts Content - TypeScript Code Display -->
    <div class="file-content" data-content="skills.ts">
      <div class="code-editor">
        <div class="code-content">
